Interpretation
--------------
cp5 / cp6       : Same patterns as 2026-05-22 and earlier 2026-05-24 runs.
                  Sub-µV noise floor at 400 SPS / PGA bypass, ~740 µV
                  post-PGA offset constant across gains.

cp7             : AIN-pair scan retires the legacy AIN2/3 saturation
                  question. ALL 8 configs (4 differential + 4 single-ended)
                  PASS. Codes range ±9M to ±893M, well below ±2^30
                  saturation. High floating-input RMS (3–31 mV) is mains/EMI
                  pickup — expected and acceptable. Single-ended readings
                  consistently land at ~-2.15 V (floating AIN ≈ 0.35 V vs
                  AINCOM @ 2.5 V VBIAS).

cp8             : ADC2 noise floor 8.5 µV, below datasheet typical of
                  10.3 µV (Table 8-3, 100 SPS, Sinc3, gain=1). Secondary
                  ADC verified working on EVM — UNBLOCKS SensorHub_PIO's
                  dual-ADC mode.

cp9             : 4007 / 4000 expected (0.175% over). PC_6 supports
                  falling-edge interrupts cleanly. Interrupt-driven reads
                  are viable on the Mid Carrier — RETIRES the legacy
                  PJ_11 / LoRa IRQ conflict workaround.

cp10            : Ratiometric TDAC sweep. AVDD derived from 5 non-offset
                  rows: 5.193 to 5.218 V, mean 5.2056 V, span 24.9 mV.
                  - Consistency check (span < 50 mV): PASS — TDAC + ADC1
                    chain is linear across the input range.
                  - Spec check (AVDD in 5.0 ± 0.25 V): PASS — EVM's
                    TPS7A4700 LDO output is in spec.
                  - Free bonus: we now have a precise measurement of the
                    EVM's actual AVDD = 5.2056 V (use this for any
                    downstream calibration math that depends on supply).
                  Offset row (0.5·AVDD, diff=0): 1.64 mV, matches the
                  chip's intrinsic offset pattern from cp5/cp6.


Bug found and fixed during this session
---------------------------------------
1. cp8 was originally configured with ADC2MUX = 0x4A (AIN4 vs AINCOM),
   intending to measure a floating pin via ADC2. That picked up ~167 mV
   RMS of mains EMI on a 100 µV threshold check → spurious FAIL.
   Fixed by changing ADC2MUX to 0xAA (AINCOM-shorted, matching cp5/cp6's
   ADC1 noise floor methodology) and bumping the threshold to 100 µV
   (10× datasheet typical for ADC2 at 100 SPS gain 1).

2. cp10 originally compared measured differential to nominal values from
   the datasheet table assuming AVDD = 5.000 V exactly. The TDAC outputs
   are NOT absolute — datasheet §9.3.14 says "The TDAC reference voltage
   is the analog supply (V_AVDD − V_AVSS); therefore, the output levels
   refer to, and scale with, the analog power supply." With AVDD = 5.21 V
   on this EVM, the measured values were ~4% above the assumed nominals,
   producing spurious FAILs on the high-magnitude rows.
   Fixed by switching to ratiometric AVDD derivation (back-compute AVDD
   from each row, check consistency across rows and spec compliance).
   This is both more diagnostic AND more correct.


